.TH STARHEX 1 "November 2026" "starhex 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
starhex \- ultra-fast versatile CLI number base, hex & encoding toolkit for Arch Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B starhex
[\fIINPUT\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B echo
\fIINPUT\fR |
.B starhex
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B starhex
is a lightning-fast command-line tool designed for Arch Linux to convert and inspect numbers, strings, binary data, colors, IP addresses, IEEE-754 floats, and Unix timestamps across arbitrary number bases and formats with automatic input detection.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t \fIBASE\fR
Target base or format. Examples: \fB\-t2\fR, \fB\-t8\fR, \fB\-t10\fR, \fB\-t16\fR, \fB\-tb\fR, \fB\-to\fR, \fB\-td\fR, \fB\-tx\fR, \fB\-ts\fR, \fB\-tb64\fR, \fB\-trgb\fR, \fB\-tip\fR, \fB\-tfloat\fR, \fB\-tdouble\fR, \fB\-ttime\fR.
.TP
.BR \-f \fIBASE\fR
Force source base or format (e.g. \fB\-f2\fR, \fB\-f16\fR, \fB\-fstr\fR).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prefix
Add base prefix (\fB0x\fR, \fB0b\fR, \fB0o\fR, \fB#\fR).
.TP
.BR \-np ", " \-\-no\-prefix
Omit base prefix (default when \-t is specified).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-upper
Output uppercase hex/alphanumeric digits.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-lower
Output lowercase hex/alphanumeric digits.
.TP
.BR \-w \fIN\fR ", " \-\-width \fIN\fR
Zero-pad output string to \fIN\fR digits / bit width.
.TP
.BR \-g \fIN\fR ", " \-\-group \fIN\fR
Group output digits into chunks of \fIN\fR separated by spaces.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Output only the converted value without decorative headers.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Display the multi-base inspection dashboard.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-color
Force ANSI color output.
.TP
.BR \-nc ", " \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI color output.
.TP
.BR \-e16 ", " \-e32 ", " \-e64
Swap byte endianness (16-bit, 32-bit, or 64-bit).
.TP
.B \-\-not
Bitwise NOT inversion.
.TP
.BR \-\-and \fIVAL\fR
Bitwise AND with \fIVAL\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-or \fIVAL\fR
Bitwise OR with \fIVAL\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-xor \fIVAL\fR
Bitwise XOR with \fIVAL\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-shl \fIN\fR
Shift left by \fIN\fR bits.
.TP
.BR \-\-shr \fIN\fR
Shift right by \fIN\fR bits.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Convert 42 from base 10 to base 2:
.B starhex 42 -t2
.TP
Convert 0x3D from hex to base 10:
.B starhex 0x3D -t10
.TP
Convert with prefix and padding:
.B starhex 42 -t2 -p -w8 -g4
.TP
Inspect multi-base dashboard:
.B starhex 0x3D
.SH AUTHOR
lovevsick
